**Business Report on Network Infrastructure Development**

As of October 2023, Nexus Communications is expanding its fiber optic network in the Greater Phoenix area to enhance mobile connectivity. This initiative aims to support the increasing data center demands driven by cloud service providers, such as DataStream Technologies, which require robust spectrum allocations for efficient operations.

| Entity                     | Type               | Status        | Dependency                  |
|---------------------------|--------------------|---------------|-----------------------------|
| Nexus Communications       | Organization       | Active        | Fiber Deployment             |
| DataStream Technologies    | Organization       | Partnership    | Data Center Capacity         |
| Greater Phoenix Area      | Location           | Target Region | Fiber Network Expansion      |
| 5G Mobile Spectrum         | Resource           | Allocated     | Mobile Service Improvement   |
| Fiber Optic Lines         | Infrastructure     | Under Construction | DataTransfer Reliability  |

Nexus Communications will collaborate with local municipalities to ensure compliance and expedite the installation process, with completion targeted for Q2 2024.